<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2015/North-Sky.jpg" alt="Painting of the north sky" width="350" height="430" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">North Sky (Large). 10x8, oil on linen panel. 2015.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Two scraped-off paintings in a row shakes an artist's confidence. Determined to avoid strike three, today I pulled out a small plein air study and painted a larger version of the thing.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">For a fresh look, I limited the working time to about the same amount as I would if I were painting outdoors. I also tried to keep some of the brush work and edges of the original study, which turned out to be a challenge.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">The view is from our back yard looking north with Camp David in the far distance. I left out a couple of pine trees on the right and a fence line to improve the composition.</p>